From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VIF1 worker thread: give it a name

What it is for:
  The optional VIF1/VU1 worker thread (patch 0034) had no name. On
  Windows a sampling profiler that picks its thread by name
  (SetThreadDescription) could not find it, and on Linux it inherited the
  name "GameThread" from the thread that starts it, so per-thread tools
  showed two "GameThread"s. In Ben 10: Protector of Earth's first level
  this worker is the busiest thread when enemies are on screen.

The change:
  The worker names itself "VIF1Worker" with ThreadNaming (as the game
  thread already names itself) before entering its loop. Nothing else
  changes.

How it was checked:
  Linux build; the name shows in top -H. ps2xTest 454/454.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include "runtime/ps2_address.h"
 #include "runtime/gs/gs_frontend.h"
 #include "ps2_log.h"
+#include "ThreadNaming.h"
 #include <atomic>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <limits>
@@ -2024,8 +2025,12 @@
         if (!m_vif1Thread.joinable())
         {
             m_vif1Quit = false;
+            // Named so that profilers and thread lists can tell it apart
+            // from the game thread that starts it (on Linux it would
+            // otherwise inherit the name "GameThread").
             m_vif1Thread = std::thread([this]()
-                                       { vif1WorkerLoop(); });
+                                       { ThreadNaming::SetCurrentThreadName("VIF1Worker");
+                                         vif1WorkerLoop(); });
         }
     }
     m_vif1Cv.notify_all();
